# 🧪 BUG — Tests & Features Guide

This file documents **every feature** of the BUG extension and all the **tests** you should run to verify them.  
Complete the **Calibration** steps first — most tests depend on calibrated head tracking and mouth detection.

---

## 📋 Prerequisites (before any test)

1. **Chrome Dev / Canary** (v128+) with the following flags enabled:
   - `chrome://flags/#optimization-guide-on-device-model` → **Enabled BypassPerfRequirement**
   - `chrome://flags/#prompt-api-for-gemini-nano` → **Enabled**
   - `chrome://flags/#summarization-api-for-gemini-nano` → **Enabled**
   - Restart Chrome after changing flags.
2. **Extension loaded**: `chrome://extensions` → Developer Mode → Load unpacked → select the repo root.
3. **Camera permission granted**: click the BUG icon and allow webcam access.
4. **AI model ready**: run `await ai.summarizer.availability()` in DevTools console — must return `"readily"`.

---

## 🎛️ Calibration Steps (MUST DO BEFORE TESTING)

### Step 1 — Head Tracking Calibration (`Alt+H`)

This maps your natural head movement range to screen coordinates.

| Pose | Action |
|------|--------|
| 1. **CENTER** | Look straight ahead → press **Space** |
| 2. **LEFT** | Rotate head gently left → press **Space** |
| 3. **RIGHT** | Rotate head gently right → press **Space** |
| 4. **UP** | Nod head slightly up → press **Space** |
| 5. **DOWN** | Nod head slightly down → press **Space** |
| 6. **CENTER AGAIN** | Return to neutral → press **Space** to finish |

> **Tips:**  
> - Good front-facing lighting makes a big difference.  
> - Keep your torso stable; move only your head.  
> - Each step captures 4–120 samples over 1.5 s — hold still until you hear the step advance.  
> - Calibration is stored as `headCalV2` in `chrome.storage.local` and persists across sessions.

### Step 2 — Mouth Click Calibration (`Alt+M`)

This teaches the extension your open/closed mouth ratio.

1. Toggle **"Enable Mouth Click"** in the side panel.
2. Press **Alt+M** (or click **"Calibrate Mouth Click"** in the panel).
3. **Step A — Closed**: keep your mouth closed when prompted. The system collects baseline samples.
4. **Step B — Open**: open your mouth wide when prompted. Samples are collected and a threshold is computed.
5. After calibration the data is stored as `mouthCalV1`.

> **Tips:**  
> - Exaggerate the open position during calibration for reliable detection.  
> - Ensure the camera can see your mouth clearly.

### Step 3 — Blink Calibration (automatic / inline)

The blink calibration runs inline when head tracking starts:

1. Keep your eyes open for ~1 second.
2. Close them gently for ~0.7 s.
3. The extension stores thresholds as `earCalV2`, enabling:
   - **Long blink ≥ 1 s** → left click
   - **Long blink ≥ 2 s** → right click

---

## 🌟 Features List

### 1. Hands-Free Control
| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Head Tracking** | Nose-vs-eye face features drive cursor position with One-Euro filtering |
| **Mouth-Open Click** | Open mouth → triggers click (800 ms cooldown prevents double-clicks) |
| **Dwell Activation** | Hover 600 ms on any link → automatic click; growing ring indicator |
| **Magnetic Snapping** | Cursor snaps to nearby clickables within 45 px radius |
| **Auto-Scroll Zones** | Look at top / bottom 180 px edge → page scrolls |
| **Navigation Zones** | Look at left 80 px edge → browser back; right 80 px → forward |

### 2. AI-Powered Link Previews
| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Web Article Summaries** | Readability.js extracts content → Chrome Summarizer API → streaming tooltip |
| **YouTube Video Summaries** | XHR intercept captures captions (JSON3 / XML) → Prompt API → structured summary |
| **Reddit Discussion Summaries** | Hover a Reddit post → comment-driven summary via "Summarizing Reddit discussion…" |
| **Twitter/X Conversation Summaries** | Hover a tweet → background tab captures GraphQL conversation → summary |
| **Smart Caching** | Summaries cached for 30 minutes |
| **Dual Display** | Show summaries in tooltip, side panel, or both |
| **Streaming Output** | Real-time character-by-character updates while AI generates |

### 3. Customization & Settings
| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Adjustable dwell time | 300–1500 ms via side panel slider |
| Head calibration | 5-point personalization (`Alt+H`) |
| Mouth calibration | Adaptive thresholds (`Alt+M`) |
| Display modes | Tooltip / Panel / Both |
| API choice | Summarizer API or custom Prompt API |
| Enhanced Dwell Sensitivity | New Update — finer control over dwell responsiveness |

### 4. Privacy & Performance
- 100 % local processing (no external servers)
- Webcam-based (any standard camera)
- GPU-accelerated tracking (WebGL)
- Lightweight (~2 MB extension)
- Works offline after initial model download

---

## 🧪 All Tests

### T01 — Head Tracking Cursor Movement
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Head calibration completed (`Alt+H`) |
| **Steps** | 1. Enable head tracking in side panel. 2. Look left / right / up / down. |
| **Expected** | Cursor moves smoothly across the viewport without excessive jitter. |
| **Verify** | One-Euro filter params: `fc=0.4`, `β=0.0025`, `d_cutoff=1.0`. |

### T02 — Mouth-Open Click
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Mouth calibration completed (`Alt+M`), "Enable Mouth Click" toggled ON |
| **Steps** | 1. Move cursor over a clickable element. 2. Open mouth. |
| **Expected** | A single click fires. No double-click within the 800 ms cooldown window. |
| **Verify** | Visual feedback appears on click. |

### T03 — Dwell Activation
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Head tracking active |
| **Steps** | 1. Hover cursor over a link for ~600 ms. |
| **Expected** | Growing ring indicator completes → click fires. |
| **Verify** | Adjusting dwell time slider (300–1500 ms) changes the activation delay. |

### T04 — Magnetic Snapping
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Head tracking active |
| **Steps** | 1. Move cursor near (within 45 px) a clickable link/button. |
| **Expected** | Cursor snaps onto the target element. |

### T05 — Auto-Scroll Zones
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Head tracking active, page is scrollable |
| **Steps** | 1. Look at the top 180 px of the viewport → page scrolls up. 2. Look at the bottom 180 px → page scrolls down. |
| **Expected** | Smooth continuous scrolling while gaze remains in the zone. Colored visual feedback appears. |

### T06 — Browser Navigation Zones
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Head tracking active, browser history exists |
| **Steps** | 1. Look at the left 80 px edge → browser goes back. 2. Look at the right 80 px edge → browser goes forward. |
| **Expected** | Navigation fires; colored zone overlay visible. |

### T07 — Long-Blink Click
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Blink calibration done (`earCalV2` stored) |
| **Steps** | 1. Close eyes ≥ 1 s → left click. 2. Close eyes ≥ 2 s → right click. |
| **Expected** | Synthetic clicks land on the sticky target under the cursor. |

### T08 — Web Article AI Summary
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | AI model ready (`"readily"`), extension loaded |
| **Steps** | 1. Open any long article (e.g., Wikipedia). 2. Hover over a link for ~600 ms. |
| **Expected** | Tooltip streams a markdown key-point summary. Side panel shows the same content if dual display is on. |
| **Verify** | Console logs show `FETCH_CONTENT` → `SUMMARIZE_CONTENT` pipeline. |

### T09 — YouTube Caption Extraction & Summary
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | AI model ready, extension loaded |
| **Steps** | 1. Open YouTube. 2. Dwell on a video thumbnail. |
| **Expected** | Captions are captured (JSON3 or XML format) → streamed summary appears in tooltip. |
| **Sample Video IDs** | `dQw4w9WgXcQ`, `jNQXAC9IVRw`, `9bZkp7q19f0` |
| **Test Harness** | Open `test/youtube-test.html` locally or via `python3 -m http.server 8000`. Run **Direct API** and **Method 4 (Network Intercept)** scenarios. Confirm all three sample IDs succeed. |

### T10 — YouTube Test Page — Direct API
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | `test/youtube-test.html` served locally |
| **Steps** | 1. Select a video ID (or enter a custom one). 2. Click **"Test Direct API"**. 3. Click **"Test All Videos"**. |
| **Expected** | Statistics update; console shows fetched captions and success/failure per video. |

### T11 — YouTube Test Page — Method 4 (Network Intercept)
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | `test/youtube-test.html` served locally |
| **Steps** | 1. Click **"Setup Intercept"**. 2. Open YouTube in a new tab and hover over thumbnails. |
| **Expected** | Captions are captured automatically; `method4-status` updates with results. |

### T12 — Reddit Hover Summary
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | AI model ready, extension loaded |
| **Steps** | 1. Browse `reddit.com` hot posts (mix of self and link posts). 2. Hover a post link. |
| **Expected** | Tooltip shows "Summarizing Reddit discussion…" state → produces comment-driven output. |
| **Edge Case** | If the thread has no accessible comments, capture console errors and verify graceful fallback. |

### T13 — Twitter/X Conversation Summary
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | AI model ready, extension loaded |
| **Steps** | 1. Load a Twitter/X conversation. 2. Hover the main tweet. 3. Hover a reply tweet. |
| **Expected** | Tooltip briefly shows "Opening conversation…" → full summary appears. |
| **Verify** | First hover spawns a muted background tab that closes automatically. Service worker console shows `"Background capture nodes"` logs with multiple tweets. |

### T14 — Summary Cancellation (`Esc`)
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Steps** | 1. Hover a link to start a summary. 2. Press **Esc** mid-run. |
| **Expected** | Tooltip hides. Active YouTube capture job (if any) is aborted. |

### T15 — Cache Behaviour
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Steps** | 1. Hover a link → get a summary. 2. Move away and hover again within 30 min. |
| **Expected** | Second hover loads instantly from cache (no AI re-processing). |
| **Verify** | Console logs show cache hit. |

### T16 — Side Panel UI & Settings
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Steps** | 1. Open the BUG side panel. 2. Toggle each setting (head tracking, mouth click, display mode, API choice, dwell slider). |
| **Expected** | Each toggle takes effect immediately on the active tab. Settings persist across sessions. |

### T17 — Debug HUD & Overlays
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Shortcuts** | `Shift+H` → toggle debug HUD, `Alt+P` → toggle red pointer, `Alt+V` → toggle mirrored camera preview, `Alt+N` → toggle head-pointer mode on/off. |
| **Expected** | Each overlay renders and un-renders correctly without breaking page layout. |

### T18 — WebGazer Hover Prototype (Experimental)
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Open `test/webgazer-demo.html` inside the extension context |
| **Steps** | 1. Click **"Start Webcam Calibration"** → click each blue dot 3× times. 2. Click **"Begin Gaze Hover Mode"**. 3. Stare at a sample article card for ~750 ms. |
| **Expected** | Summary request triggers and a tooltip/placeholder appears. |

### T19 — Service Worker Resilience
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Steps** | 1. Enable intercept. 2. Exercise hover previews on a live YouTube tab. 3. Reload the service worker from `chrome://extensions`. |
| **Expected** | After reload, hover previews still work. Note browser/version and whether the service worker was reloaded. |

### T20 — Enhanced Dwell Sensitivity (New Feature)
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Steps** | 1. Open the options/side panel. 2. Adjust the dwell sensitivity slider to its minimum and maximum. 3. Hover links and observe activation speed. |
| **Expected** | Minimum setting → very fast dwell; maximum → slower, deliberate dwell. |

### T21 — Voice Commands
| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Precondition** | Voice enabled in side panel ("Enable Voice" toggle ON), microphone permission granted |
| **Steps** | 1. Say each command from the Voice Commands Reference below. 2. Verify the correct action fires. 3. Say `"help"` → TTS reads available commands. 4. Say `"search"` → TTS asks "What do you want to search?" → speak a query → Google opens. |
| **Expected** | Each command triggers the corresponding action. Voice log in the side panel shows badge (executed / heard / unknown). Duplicate commands within the same recognition cycle are ignored. |

